    "nw_biology_Q8CyJc": {
      "type": "nw-biology",
      "blocks": {
        "card_VxY9MX": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "METABOLISM",
            "title": "Pre-Diabetic in One Week",
            "description": "<p>A landmark Harvard study showed healthy young men developed pre-diabetic metabolic markers after just  one week of restricted sleep, even when eating carefully. </p>",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/Mask_group345_2_9dcf1126-7ac3-42e1-9740-c8def8c7e32d.png"
          }
        },
        "card_VXAhQc": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "LONG-TERM BRAIN HEALTH",
            "title": "A 30% Higher Dementia Risk",
            "description": "<p>A 25-year study of nearly 8,000 people linked chronic short sleep in midlife to a 30% higher dementia risk  decades later.</p>",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/Mask_group345_2_3.png"
          }
        },
        "card_qae3k9": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "BRAIN DETOX",
            "title": "Your Brain Cleans Itself at Night",
            "description": "<p>During deep sleep, the brain's glymphatic system clears out waste. Cut sleep short and that nightly clean-out never fully runs.</p>",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/Mask_group345_2_1.png"
          }
        },
        "card_hHU7KX": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "THE ENVIRONMENT",
            "title": "Your Body Wants to Heal",
            "description": "<p>\"Your body is trying to heal you. It just needs the environment.\" For Gary, sleep drives oxygen, inflammation, recovery, hormones, and cellular repair. You can't out-supplement a bad night.</p>",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/Mask_group345_2_2.png"
          }
        },
        "card_w4H9Mt": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "MUSCLE & RECOVERY",
            "title": "Muscle Repairs in Deep Sleep",
            "description": "<p>Deep sleep is where physical repair happens: growth hormone spikes, the brain detoxes, and the body rebuilds. Cut it short and recovery never fully runs.</p>",
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/Frame_2147238924.png"
          }
        },
        "card_RhwpCU": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "tag": "TESTOSTERONE",
            "title": "Testosterone Is Made at Night",
            "description": "<p>Gary is direct about it: testosterone is produced during sleep. Skip the deep, restorative hours and you undercut the hormones that drive energy, drive, and recovery.</p>",
